70992d6fe27a3aeea46bf30ca364bb98c6; src/rebar/_mcp_health.py is 712 lines and src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py is 207 lines in this checkout. Per the ticket's reviewed-source note, treat commit 952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d as the attested source baseline for the extraction. Proceeding with a handshake-only split that preserves _mcp_health as the facade, keeps _mcp_serving as the serving owner, and proves the same handshake/transport/shutdown contracts with focused tests.","timestamp":1788443072434066001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented the startup-handshake-only extraction. Added RED guards that require a separate rebar._mcp_startup_handshake leaf and prove _mcp_health re-exports the prior symbols, then moved the handshake cluster there while keeping _mcp_health as facade and _mcp_serving as the serving owner. Focused validation is green: tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py, tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py, and tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py -k 'run_http_with_grace or handshake', plus make lint and make typecheck. Broad default pytest again reached only the already-known clean-origin/main lifecycle baseline cluster in tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py. Pushed as Gerrit change 2575 from commit 05fe054348e1.","timestamp":1788444021523989001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788311273475283001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0250622a-1085-4df4-aa33-f6af5e683268","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4ccd-6a86-de5f-43f3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate source is commit `952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d`. At that commit, `git show 952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d:src/rebar/_mcp_health.py | wc -l` reports 712 lines. It owns startup handshake, health routing, in-flight instrumentation, and startup checks. The separate `src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py` is 207 lines. It owns `run_mcp`, `run_http_with_grace`, SIGTERM handling, and shutdown. `_mcp_health` re-exports that serving cluster at its file end. `_mcp_serving` imports `install_startup_handshake` from `_mcp_health` and calls it before uvicorn serves.\n\n## End State\n\nA leaf `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` owns only the cohesive initialize-probe call graph: probe-host selection, ASGI request drive, bounded result record, lifespan wrapping, and handshake status. `_mcp_health` remains the health facade. It re-exports existing handshake names. `_mcp_serving` remains the serving facade. It retains HTTP transport, SIGTERM draining, and the existing `install_startup_handshake` call through `_mcp_health`. `mcp_server.py` retains facade-level imports.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Before coding, recensus the checkout. Record on this ticket the HEAD SHA, the line counts, and the command output above. Treat `952f...` as the reviewed-source attestation.\n2. Move the handshake-only cluster into `_mcp_startup_handshake.py`. The new leaf must not import `_mcp_health` or `_mcp_serving`.\n3. Import plus re-export handshake names through `_mcp_health` before its existing end-of-file serving re-export. Preserve current direct imports and monkeypatch targets.\n4. Keep `_mcp_serving` as the only owner of `run_mcp`, `run_http_with_grace`, `make_sigterm_handler`, and `drain_then_exit`. Preserve its `_mcp_health.install_startup_handshake` import/call shape so the established import cycle remains acyclic.\n5. Do not move health routing, gauge instrumentation, startup store/op-cert checks, HTTP transport, SIGTERM drainage, or shutdown behavior.\n6. Prove the handshake success, non-200, exception, timeout, host selection, lifespan ordering, facade re-export, transport, and shutdown contracts with focused tests.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_startup_handshake.py` — new handshake-only leaf\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — health facade imports plus handshake re-exports\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py` — preserved serving import/call seam plus re-export-cycle contract\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — only if facade import/annotation verification requires a change\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py` — handshake result and facade compatibility\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py` — pre-serve handshake, HTTP transport, and graceful-shutdown behavior\n\nCascade flag: true. Re-run semantic, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch consumer census at implementation start.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The implementation ticket comment records the current HEAD SHA.\n- [x] The comment records `_mcp_health.py` plus `_mcp_serving.py` line counts.\n- [x] The comment records the gate-pinned `952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d` source attestation.\n- [x] Only the startup-handshake call graph moves into `_mcp_startup_handshake.py`.\n- [x] `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` has no import of `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` has no import of `_mcp_serving`.\n- [x] `_mcp_health` re-exports every existing handshake name.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `run_mcp`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `run_http_with_grace`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `make_sigterm_handler`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` keeps `drain_then_exit`.\n- [x] `_mcp_serving` retains its `install_startup_handshake` call through `_mcp_health` before uvicorn serves.\n- [x] Existing direct imports plus monkeypatch targets continue resolving through `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] Handshake success preserves its result record.\n- [x] Handshake non-200 preserves its result record.\n- [x] Handshake exception preserves its result record.\n- [x] Handshake timeout preserves its result record.\n- [x] Public-host selection preserves its existing output.\n- [x] Lifespan ordering preserves pre-serve handshake execution.\n- [x] Health routing remains in `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] Gauge instrumentation remains in `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] Startup store/op-cert checks remain in `_mcp_health`.\n- [x] HTTP transport remains in `_mcp_serving`.\n- [x] SIGTERM draining remains in `_mcp_serving`.\n- [x] Focused MCP unit tests pass.\n- [x] Focused MCP facade tests pass.\n- [x] Module-size checks pass.\n- [x] Complexity checks pass.\n- [x] Lint passes.\n- [x] Typecheck passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","reason":"extract only the startup-handshake call graph and retain facade wiring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_startup_handshake.py","reason":"new focused owner for the existing handshake cluster"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"preserve server wiring if import ownership changes"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py","reason":"prove startup success/failure and ordering"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py","reason":"guard health-route and store-state behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","4ccd-6a86-de5f-43f3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"e82575ab-5824-4007-a8de-bc8c702c0a29","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","mcp","refactor","rp07"],"ticket_id":"4ac6-9eb3-b0a5-408f","ticket_type":"story","title":"Extract only the MCP startup-handshake call-graph unit","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1eb24d39-a06a-4516-8424-7c73da75e975","7a85b5d4-cdd7-4fe6-9654-e51a8b0038bf","1222374b-b04d-492a-aa64-d02882c93528","099f5d9d-f3c4-4cd4-88f8-73c8a3ddbead","7ba3c8f7-fce1-4570-82f6-b0464f0d894d","192a39bd-5179-4601-a5f7-2467b65f4f7e","5198aac6-a3da-49f1-a8c2-a0249cb03afd","0250622a-1085-4df4-aa33-f6af5e683268","5019528d-1a0d-4520-a777-fc8eb45d96da","e82575ab-5824-4007-a8de-bc8c702c0a29","129f8a1d-2e07-4171-a646-3e27b106e87e"]},"env_i